Fillets: a rounding ending on a face at the end split round the corner's
vertex into several faces of one surface, each piece with its own
surface (mitcad#415).

The case: a bar's top edge rounded where the bar meets a bore's wall; the
wall round the corner's vertex is three faces of one cylinder (a piece
above the bar's top, one beside the bar below it and one beside it above,
as booleans that kept faces of different origins apart leave it), each on
its own cylinder object. PerformIntersectionAtEnd walks round the vertex
through the three and, the faces being tangent along both edges between
them, takes the cut on one piece (oneintersection, Face[0]); the part of
the contact's arc on another piece (edgesau, the arc on facesau) from the
contact's point to the vertex becomes the edge between them. Its curve on
Face[0] was asked of the arc (BRep_Tool::CurveOnSurface), which has curves
only on its own faces' surfaces: null where the pieces do not share the
surface object. The edge then had no curve on that face, and the arc's
point on it (Hc1, Hc2) was taken at (0, 0): the face was invalid or cut
along a wrong curve (the volume wrong).

- ChFi3d_ArcOnSameSurface: an edge's curve on a face of the same surface
  as its own faces: its 3d curve projected on the face's surface,
  parametrized as the 3d curve, moved by whole periods into the face's
  period at the vertex, and checked to lie on the surface.
- PerformIntersectionAtEnd: where the arc's curve on the face at the end
  is null (Hc1 of the first face, Hc2 of the last, C2dint1 of the edge
  between the pieces in the oneintersection case), it is computed so.

Before, the result was invalid. Test: a bar across a ring of two layers,
the upper notched over the bar and the notch filled again (the bore's wall
in three pieces round each end of the bar's top edges), as copied (each
piece on its own surface): the bar's top edges rounded (geometry
test_fillet_results).

